---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Hyphos — the engagement, apprenticed"
  description="Hyphos is the enterprise knowledge and apprenticeship layer above your operational systems. One engagement object. Deliverables that learn from your edits. Document control that runs invisibly in the channels you already use."
>

  {/* ─── Hero ─── */}
  <section class="relative min-h-[88vh] flex items-center justify-center overflow-hidden pt-24 pb-20">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-grid" />
    <div class="absolute top-1/4 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-[700px] h-[700px] bg-indigo-500/10 rounded-full blur-[140px]" />
    <div class="absolute top-1/3 left-1/3 w-[500px] h-[500px] bg-cyan-400/6 rounded-full blur-[120px]" />

    <div class="relative max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full border border-indigo-500/20 bg-indigo-500/5 text-indigo-300 text-xs font-medium mb-10">
        <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-indigo-400 animate-pulse" />
        In design partnership now — opening to a small pilot cohort
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white leading-[1.05]">
        Your organization's knowledge —<br />
        <span class="text-gradient">captured, taught, retained.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="mt-7 text-lg sm:text-xl text-slate-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
        Hyphos captures the knowledge your team is creating every day — in meetings, in documents, in the decisions they make — and teaches it back to the people who need it. It grows with the work. Unlike most systems, it's never static. And unlike most AI, the knowledge belongs to you, not the vendor.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500 max-w-xl mx-auto">
        One assistant, not a portal. Channel-native — runs inside the email, meetings, and chat your team already uses.
      </p>

      {/* Pilot CTA */}
      <form
        id="waitlist-form"
        class="mt-10 flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 max-w-md mx-auto"
        onsubmit="event.preventDefault(); const e=document.getElementById('wl-email').value; if(!e) return; window.location.href = 'mailto:hello@hyphos.io?subject=Hyphos%20pilot%20interest%20—%20' + encodeURIComponent(e) + '&body=' + encodeURIComponent('Hi — please add me (' + e + ') to the Hyphos pilot list.\\n\\nA bit about us (organization, the engagement you have in mind, what you\\'re hoping Hyphos solves):\\n\\n');"
      >
        <input
          id="wl-email"
          type="email"
          required
          placeholder="you@yourcompany.com"
          class="flex-1 px-4 py-3 text-sm rounded-lg bg-white/5 border border-white/10 text-white placeholder:text-slate-500 focus:outline-none focus:border-indigo-400/50 focus:bg-white/8"
        />
        <button
          type="submit"
          class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold rounded-lg bg-indigo-600 text-white hover:bg-indigo-500 transition-all glow-indigo"
        >
          Talk about a pilot
          <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13 7l5 5m0 0l-5 5m5-5H6" /></svg>
        </button>
      </form>
      <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-slate-600">No marketing emails. We reply to every note personally.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ─── The shift — three quick frames ─── */}
  <section class="relative border-t border-white/5 bg-slate-900/30">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-20">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto text-center mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">
          A different kind of system
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-400">
          Hyphos isn't a copilot, a chatbot, or a portal. It's an apprenticeship system that happens to produce deliverables.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-10 text-center">
        <div>
          <div class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-3">Not a copilot</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">A copilot sits beside you and suggests. Hyphos does the work, ships the artifact, and articulates the craft behind it — modeling, scaffolding, fading. Your juniors learn from the seniors they don't get enough time with.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-3">Not a portal</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">No new system to log in to. Hyphos is channel-native — it works inside the email, meeting, and chat surfaces your team already uses. Document control runs continuously in the background of how you already work.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-3">Not a system-of-record rebuild</div>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">Hyphos doesn't replace your CRM, your ERP, your scheduling system, or your document repository. It sits above them as the intelligence and apprenticeship layer that ties scope, schedule, cost, quality, and resources to the work actually happening.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ─── What it does — the four substrates ─── */}
  <section class="py-24 border-t border-white/5 relative">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto text-center mb-14">
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">
          What Hyphos actually does
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base text-slate-400">
          Four substrates, running together — quietly, in the work.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5">

        {/* Engagement */}
        <div class="glass-card rounded-xl p-7">
          <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-indigo-500/10 flex items-center justify-center text-indigo-400 mb-4">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3.75 7.5l8.25-3.75 8.25 3.75M3.75 7.5v9l8.25 3.75M3.75 7.5l8.25 3.75m0 9V11.25m0 9l8.25-3.75v-9M12 11.25l8.25-3.75"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">The engagement is the object</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
            Not projects, plus meetings, plus documents, plus tasks. One engagement — call it a matter, a case, a deal, a project, whatever your firm calls it — with the five axes that govern every complex undertaking: scope, schedule, cost, quality, resources. Everything else hangs off it.
          </p>
        </div>

        {/* Apprenticeship */}
        <div class="glass-card rounded-xl p-7">
          <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-cyan-500/10 flex items-center justify-center text-cyan-400 mb-4">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4.26 10.147a60.438 60.438 0 0 0-.491 6.347A48.62 48.62 0 0 1 12 20.904a48.62 48.62 0 0 1 8.232-4.41 60.46 60.46 0 0 0-.491-6.347m-15.482 0a50.636 50.636 0 0 0-2.658-.813A59.906 59.906 0 0 1 12 3.493a59.903 59.903 0 0 1 10.399 5.84c-.896.248-1.783.52-2.658.814m-15.482 0A50.717 50.717 0 0 1 12 13.489a50.702 50.702 0 0 1 7.74-3.342M6.75 15a.75.75 0 1 0 0-1.5.75.75 0 0 0 0 1.5Zm0 0v-3.675A55.378 55.378 0 0 1 12 8.443m-7.007 11.55A5.981 5.981 0 0 0 6.75 15.75v-1.5"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">Cognitive apprenticeship at scale</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
            The way a junior used to learn — sitting beside a senior, watching them work, getting corrected on the small moves — doesn't survive modern knowledge work. Hyphos restores it. Every deliverable ships with its developmental companion: the reasoning, the facilitator's guide, the watch-for-next-time. Modeling, scaffolding, fading, articulation — the four moves of mastery, encoded.
          </p>
        </div>

        {/* Living deliverables */}
        <div class="glass-card rounded-xl p-7">
          <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-emerald-500/10 flex items-center justify-center text-emerald-400 mb-4">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3.75 13.5l10.5-11.25L12 10.5h8.25L9.75 21.75 12 13.5H3.75z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">Living deliverables that learn from your edits</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
            Deliverables are interactive HTML by default — explored, not read. The reader controls the depth and path. PDF, DOCX, PPTX are derivative exports, made on demand. And when you correct a draft, the craft of that correction is captured — so the next proposal, the next plan, the next report inherits what your firm just learned.
          </p>
        </div>

        {/* Invisible doc control */}
        <div class="glass-card rounded-xl p-7">
          <div class="w-9 h-9 rounded-lg bg-purple-500/10 flex items-center justify-center text-purple-400 mb-4">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75 11.25 15 15 9.75M21 12a9 9 0 1 1-18 0 9 9 0 0 1 18 0Z"/></svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-white mb-2">Invisible document control</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
            Capture, classify, draft, route, approve, distribute, audit — the full document-control process, running continuously in the background of how people already work. No portal. No forms. No "submit." Replaces the legacy portal-style document-control layer rather than competing with it on its own terms.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ─── Not another data lake ─── */}
  <section class="py-24 border-t border-white/5 relative">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto text-center mb-14">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase text-indigo-400 mb-3">How it's different</p>
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">
          Not another data lake.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-base text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Every modern data platform promises the same thing: consolidate your sources into bronze, silver, gold layers and you'll finally get value. The pipelines get built. The dashboards arrive. The people doing the work see almost none of it. Hyphos is the opposite shape — a loop, not a pipeline.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">

        {/* LEFT — Lakehouse */}
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-white/8 bg-white/[0.02] p-7">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase text-slate-500 mb-2">What most platforms sell</p>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-300 mb-6">A pipeline that ends at a dashboard</h3>

          <div class="space-y-2.5 mb-5">
            {[
              { name: 'Source systems', sub: 'CRM, email, docs, meetings' },
              { name: 'Bronze · raw', sub: 'Landing zone' },
              { name: 'Silver · cleaned', sub: 'Conformed, deduplicated' },
              { name: 'Gold · curated', sub: 'Business-ready tables' },
              { name: 'BI dashboard', sub: 'Insights, theoretically' },
            ].map((stage, i, arr) => (
              <div>
                <div class={`rounded-lg border border-white/8 bg-slate-900/40 px-4 py-2.5 ${i === arr.length - 1 ? 'border-dashed' : ''}`}>
                  <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-300">{stage.name}</p>
                  <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-0.5">{stage.sub}</p>
                </div>
                {i < arr.length - 1 && (
                  <div class="flex justify-center py-1">
                    <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-slate-600" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg>
                  </div>
                )}
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>

          <div class="border-t border-white/5 pt-4 space-y-1.5 text-xs text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">
            <p><span class="text-slate-400 font-medium">One-way.</span> Source → dashboard. Nothing flows back.</p>
            <p><span class="text-slate-400 font-medium">Static.</span> Patterns don't learn from edits. Templates rot.</p>
            <p><span class="text-slate-400 font-medium">Years to value.</span> Pipelines, modeling, governance, training.</p>
            <p><span class="text-slate-400 font-medium">Insights stranded.</span> The craft of the seniors never makes it back into the work.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        {/* RIGHT — Hyphos architecture */}
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-indigo-500/40 bg-indigo-950/40 p-7 shadow-xl shadow-indigo-500/10 relative">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase text-indigo-300 mb-2">What Hyphos is</p>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-6">An architecture between work and record</h3>

          {/* Top layer: where the work happens */}
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-cyan-500/30 bg-cyan-500/[0.06] px-4 py-3">
            <p class="text-[10px] font-bold tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-cyan-300/80 mb-1">Where the work happens</p>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">Meetings · Email · Chat · Documents</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-cyan-200/60 mt-1">Channel-native — no portal to learn, no new place to log in</p>
          </div>

          {/* Down + up arrows — capture + deliver */}
          <div class="flex justify-center items-center gap-4 py-2.5">
            <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-0.5">
              <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-indigo-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 14l-7 7m0 0l-7-7m7 7V3"/></svg>
              <span class="text-[9px] font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-indigo-400/70">Capture</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-0.5">
              <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-indigo-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 10l7-7m0 0l7 7m-7-7v18"/></svg>
              <span class="text-[9px] font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-indigo-400/70">Deliver</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          {/* Middle layer: HYPHOS — the named components */}
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-indigo-400/40 bg-indigo-950/70 p-4">
            <p class="text-[10px] font-bold tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-indigo-300 mb-3 text-center">Hyphos</p>
            <div class="space-y-1.5">
              <div class="rounded-md bg-indigo-900/40 border border-indigo-500/25 px-3 py-2">
                <p class="text-xs font-bold text-white">Engagement spine</p>
                <p class="text-[11px] text-indigo-200/70 leading-snug">One object · scope · schedule · cost · quality · resources</p>
              </div>
              <div class="rounded-md bg-indigo-900/40 border border-indigo-500/25 px-3 py-2">
                <p class="text-xs font-bold text-white">Knowledge graph + shared ontology</p>
                <p class="text-[11px] text-indigo-200/70 leading-snug">Typed entities · full provenance · one vocabulary across sources</p>
              </div>
              <div class="rounded-md bg-indigo-900/40 border border-indigo-500/25 px-3 py-2">
                <p class="text-xs font-bold text-white">Depth stack</p>
                <p class="text-[11px] text-indigo-200/70 leading-snug">Universal · industry · organization · engagement · live signal</p>
              </div>
              <div class="rounded-md bg-indigo-900/40 border border-indigo-500/25 px-3 py-2">
                <p class="text-xs font-bold text-white">Apprenticeship engine</p>
                <p class="text-[11px] text-indigo-200/70 leading-snug">Model · scaffold · fade · articulate — the four moves of craft</p>
              </div>
              <div class="rounded-md bg-indigo-900/40 border border-indigo-500/25 px-3 py-2">
                <p class="text-xs font-bold text-white">Living templates + audit</p>
                <p class="text-[11px] text-indigo-200/70 leading-snug">Templates mature with use · every change provenanced</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          {/* Down + up arrows — reads + writes */}
          <div class="flex justify-center items-center gap-4 py-2.5">
            <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-0.5">
              <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-indigo-400/60" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M19 14l-7 7m0 0l-7-7m7 7V3"/></svg>
              <span class="text-[9px] font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-indigo-400/60">Reads</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-0.5">
              <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-indigo-400/60" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 10l7-7m0 0l7 7m-7-7v18"/></svg>
              <span class="text-[9px] font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-indigo-400/60">Writes</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          {/* Bottom layer: systems of record */}
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-500/30 bg-slate-500/[0.06] px-4 py-3 mb-5">
            <p class="text-[10px] font-bold tracking-[0.2em] uppercase text-slate-400 mb-1">Your systems of record</p>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-200">CRM · ERP · Scheduling · Doc repository · Foundation</p>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-1">Hyphos reads from and writes to — never replaces</p>
          </div>

          <div class="border-t border-indigo-500/20 pt-4 space-y-1.5 text-xs text-indigo-100/70 leading-relaxed">
            <p><span class="text-white font-medium">Sits between work and record.</span> Not a portal. Not a replacement.</p>
            <p><span class="text-white font-medium">Living.</span> Templates mature with use. Nothing static.</p>
            <p><span class="text-white font-medium">Quick to value.</span> Channel-native — integrations layer in alongside, never as a prerequisite.</p>
            <p><span class="text-white font-medium">Knowledge retained.</span> Yours, with full provenance.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 text-center">
        <a href="/architecture" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm font-semibold text-indigo-300 hover:text-indigo-200 transition-colors">
          See the depths, the ontology, the knowledge packs
          <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3"/></svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ─── The mutual loop ─── */}
  <section class="py-24 border-t border-white/5 relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute top-1/2 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 w-[600px] h-[600px] bg-indigo-500/8 rounded-full blur-[140px]" />
    <div class="relative max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase text-indigo-400 mb-5">The mutual loop</p>
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white leading-tight">
        The system learns from the work.<br />
        Your team learns from the system.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-7 text-base sm:text-lg text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
        Most software optimizes for capture or for output. Hyphos optimizes for the loop between them — every artifact produced is also an act of teaching, every edit corrected is also an act of learning. Neither direction is the product alone. The product is the mutual loop running.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ─── Hyphos + Foundation ─── */}
  <section class="py-24 border-t border-white/5 relative">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto text-center mb-14">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase text-indigo-400 mb-3">Two products, one company</p>
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">
          Hyphos + Foundation
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-base text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
          Hyphos is one of two products from Hyphos Consulting. <strong class="text-white">Foundation</strong> is the integrated operating system that runs your business — customer, calendar, financials, documents, communications, all on one shared database. <strong class="text-white">Hyphos</strong> is the knowledge and apprenticeship layer that sits above your operational systems and turns the work happening there into captured craft.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-5">
        {/* Foundation */}
        <div class="glass-card rounded-2xl p-7 relative">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase text-cyan-400">Foundation</p>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase text-slate-500">Operational layer</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-3">The business, integrated</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed mb-5">
            One shared database for customer, calendar, financials, documents, and audit. Sixteen integrated modules across front of house, back of house, finance, and growth — shaped to the industry you're in. Replaces the patchwork of 8–12 disconnected subscriptions most organizations are stitching together.
          </p>
          <a href="https://hyphosconsulting.com/products#foundation" class="text-sm text-cyan-300 hover:text-cyan-200 transition-colors inline-flex items-center gap-1.5">
            See Foundation
            <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3"/></svg>
          </a>
        </div>

        {/* Hyphos */}
        <div class="rounded-2xl p-7 border border-indigo-500/40 bg-indigo-950/60 shadow-xl shadow-indigo-500/10 relative">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase text-indigo-300">Hyphos</p>
            <span class="text-[10px] font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase text-indigo-300/70">Knowledge layer</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-3">The craft, captured</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed mb-5">
            Sits above the operational systems your organization already runs — Foundation, or any combination of your existing CRM, ERP, scheduling, and document systems. Produces the deliverables, captures the expertise, develops the people through the work itself. Built for the engagements where the cost of getting it wrong is high and the seniors who know how to get it right are too scarce.
          </p>
          <span class="text-sm text-indigo-300 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-medium">
            You are here
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-10 text-center text-xs text-slate-500 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
